{"cuisine/sakhalin-korean-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/sakhalin-korean-cuisine","n":"Sakhalin Korean cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine"],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in South Korea","intro":[["Sakhalin Koreans are a group of ethnic Koreans on the island of Sakhalin, Russia. They have a distinct style of cuisine that descends from Korean cuisine and Russian cuisine. They are often considered distinct from Koryo-saram, Koreans of the former Soviet Union, who have their own cuisine."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"sakhalin-korean-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sakhalin_Korean_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine"],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine"],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine"},"dish/bakakak-hayam":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/bakakak-hayam","n":"Bakakak hayam","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Bakakak hayam or Ayam Bekakak (Ayam Bekakak, Bakakak chicken or Splayed chicken) is a traditional Sundanese cuisine, originating from the  Indonesia. The form of chicken roasted above fire, after it is cleaned and added with special seasonings. Usually a chef uses a bamboo stick to grab a chicken to make it easy to grill. This dish will usually be served during a Sundanese wedding procession."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-bakakak-hayam"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bakakak_hayam"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","ref":"site/dailycookingquest-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"si